            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A memory structure stores a plurality of color maps, the entity, when decompressed by a printer controller, comprising a plurality of first level wrappers, each first level wrapper including at least one characteristic to identify a corresponding color map, and a recipe to define and locate packets for constructing the color map, the recipe having at least one locator for each second level wrapper ; and a plurality of second level wrappers of different types, each second level wrapper wrapping a corresponding packet.</p>
